    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need help with some catering stuff for a big gala we're doing next month. it's for a law firm, like 500 people. we just got a bunch of emails about severe nut allergies and some vegans. what's the best way to tell the kitchen staff so nothing gets missed and how should we label the buffet so people don't accidentally eat something they shouldn't?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For communicating with the kitchen, create a comprehensive allergy matrix listing all known severe allergies and dietary restrictions, clearly marking required cross-contamination protocols. Ensure this document is prominently displayed and reviewed by the head chef before service begins. For the buffet, utilize clear, large signage for every dish indicating major allergens (like nuts, dairy, and gluten) and a dedicated tag for vegan options. This double-layer approach—kitchen notification and guest labeling—will ensure safety and clarity for all attendees.",
